<<<
+ of the kingdom is represented by the majority in another part./In England the very completeness of the defeat of Roman Catholicism has rendered the people oblivious to the danger of its aggression.
===
+ *of the kingdom is represented by the majority in another part.*/*In England the very completeness of the defeat of Roman Catholicism has rendered the people oblivious to the danger of its aggression.*
>>>

<<<
The making of these mistakes is part of the price paid by those who reject the homely word, avoid the obvious, & look about for the imposing; forgetful, unaware, unconscious, unmindful, & insensible, while they usually give the meaning more precisely, lay no traps.
===
The making of these mistakes is part of the price paid by those who reject the homely word, avoid the obvious, & look about for the imposing; *forgetful, unaware, unconscious, unmindful,* & *insensible,* while they usually give the meaning more precisely, lay no traps.
>>>

<<<
obnoxious has two very different senses, one of which (exposed or open or liable to attack or injury) requires notice because its currency is now so restricted that it is puzzling to the uninstructed.
===
**obnoxious** has two very different senses, one of which (exposed or open or liable *to* attack or injury) requires notice because its currency is now so restricted that it is puzzling to the uninstructed.
>>>

<<<
It is the word’s rightful or de-jure meaning, & we may hope that scholarly writers will keep it alive, as they have hitherto succeeded in doing.
===
It is the word's rightful or *de-jure* meaning, & we may hope that scholarly writers will keep it alive, as they have hitherto succeeded in doing.
>>>

<<<
Meanwhile the rest of us need not scruple to recognize the usurping or de-facto sense offensive or objectionable;
===
Meanwhile the rest of us need not scruple to recognize the usurping or *de-facto* sense offensive or objectionable;
>>>

<<<
oboe. See HAUTBOY.
===
**oboe.** See ^^HAUTBOY^^.
