<<<
obstacle. Their apathy, fatalism, & resentment of interference constituted, & still constitute, a formidable obstacle of progress. After obstacle, idiom requires to, not of.
===
**obstacle.** *Their apathy, fatalism, & resentment of interference constituted, & still constitute, a formidable* obstacle *of progress.* After *obstacle*, idiom requires *to*, not *of*.
>>>

<<<
obstetric(al). See -ic(au). The short form is much commoner, & is recommended; its formation is in fact faulty (a midwife is obstetria, -icis, so that obstetricic would be the true adjective), while that of obstetrical would pass;
===
**obstetric(al).** See ^^-IC(AL)^^. The short form is much commoner, & is recommended; its formation is in fact faulty (a midwife is *obstetrix*, *-īcis*, so that *obstetricic* would be the true adjective), while that of *obstetrical* would pass;
>>>

